[93.856054, "o", "\u001b[?2026h\u001b7\u001b[2;77H\u001b[38;5;210m\u2584\u001b[38;5;210m\u2580\u001b[38;5;210m\u2588 \u001b[38;5;216m\u2588\u001b[38;5;216m\u2580\u001b[38;5;216m\u2584\u001b[38;5;216m\u2580\u001b[38;5;216m\u2588 \u001b[38;5;216m\u2580\u001b[38;5;222m\u2588\u001b[38;5;222m\u2580\u001b[0m\u001b[3;77H\u001b[38;5;210m\u2588\u001b[38;5;210m\u2580\u001b[38;5;210m\u2588 \u001b[38;5;216m\u2588 \u001b[38;5;216m\u2580 \u001b[38;5;216m\u2588 \u001b[38;5;222m\u2584\u001b[38;5;222m\u2588\u001b[38;5;222m\u2584\u001b[0m\u001b[4;77H\u001b]8;;https://www.superinference.org\u0007\u001b[2mwww.superinference.org\u001b[22m\u001b]8;;\u0007\u001b[0m\u001b8"]
[93.856492, "o", "\u001b[29A\u001b[1G\u001b[KA couple of results worth verifying by eye:\r\r\n\u001b[1G\u001b[K\r\r\n\u001b[1G\u001b[K\u2022 report_?????.pdf matched only report_final.pdf because final is exactly 5 chars \u2014 each ? consumes\r\r\n\u001b[1G\u001b[Kone. A 6-char stem would fail.\r\r\n\u001b[1G\u001b[K\u2022 ???es.txt matched notes.txt: not fills the three ?, then es.txt matches literally.\r\r\n\u001b[1G\u001b[K\r\r\n\u001b[1G\u001b[K\u001b[1mHow the DP works:\u001b[22m dp[i][j] answers \"do the first i chars of the filename match the first j chars of\r\r\n\u001b[1G\u001b[Kthe pattern?\" The whole algorithm hinges on the * recurrence \u2014 a * either matches \u001b[3mnothing\u001b[23m\r\r\n\u001b[1G\u001b[K(dp[i][j-1], skip the star) or \u001b[3mconsumes one more character\u001b[23m and stays available (dp[i-1][j]). That\r\r\n\u001b[1G\u001b[Ksingle OR is what lets one * absorb an arbitrary-length run without backtracking.\r\r\n\u001b[1G\u001b[K\r\r\n\u001b[1G\u001b[K\u2605 Insight \u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\r\r\n\u001b[1G\u001b[K- The `*` case is the only one that references the same row (`dp[i-1][j]`) rather than only the\r\r\n\u001b[1G\u001b[Kdiagonal/previous column \u2014 that self-reference is what encodes \"zero or more\" greedily yet\r\r\n\u001b[1G\u001b[Kcorrectly, avoiding the exponential backtracking a naive recursive matcher suffers.\r\r\n\u001b[1G\u001b[K- Separating `is_match` (pure logic) from `main.py` (I/O + formatting) keeps the matcher\r\r\n\u001b[1G\u001b[Kindependently testable \u2014 the printing concerns never leak into the algorithm.\r\r\n\u001b[1G\u001b[K\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\